To create a text editor with multiple lists using Angular, you can follow these steps:

1. **Set Up Your Project:**
   First, ensure you have an Angular project set up and installed. If not, use the following command to create a new Angular application:
   ```bash
   ng new my-text-editor-app
   cd my-text-editor-app
   ```

2. **Create Components:**
   Create two components for your text editor and list management. For example, `TextEditorComponent` and `ListManagementComponent`.

3. **Text Editor Component (`TextEditorComponent`):**
   This component will handle the editing functionality of the text area.

4. **List Management Component (`ListManagementComponent`):**
   This component will manage the lists that the user can add or delete from the text editor.

5. **Data Binding and State Management:**
   Use Angular's data binding capabilities to bind the state of the text editor to the UI. Also, manage the state of the lists (e.g., adding/removing items) within the same component.

6. **UI Structure:**
   Design the UI structure where the text area is at one side and a list of items appears on the other side. Use Angular directives like `*ngFor` to display each item in the list.

7. **Routing:**
   Optionally, if you want different pages based on the current view (text editor vs. list management), consider setting up routing.

8. **Testing:**
   Test both components thoroughly to make sure they work as expected.

### Example Code

Here’s a simple implementation outline:

#### 1. Text Editor Component (`src/app/text-editor.component.ts`)

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-text-editor',
  templateUrl: './text-editor.component.html',
  styleUrls: ['./text-editor.component.css']
})
export class TextEditorComponent {
  // Sample text content
  textContent = '';

  // Function to update the text content
  updateTextContent(content: string) {
    this.textContent = content;
  }

  // Function to toggle the visibility of the list
  toggleListVisibility() {
    const listContainer = document.getElementById('list-container');
    listContainer.style.display = listContainer.style.display === 'none' ? 'block' : 'none';
  }
}
```

#### 2. List Management Component (`src/app/list-management.component.ts`)

```typescript
import { Component } from '@angular/core';

@Component({
  selector: 'app-list-management',
  templateUrl: './list-management.component.html'
})
export class ListManagementComponent {
  // Sample list items
  listItems = ['Item 1', 'Item 2'];

  // Function to add a new item
  addItem(item: string) {
    this.listItems.push(item);
  }

  // Function to remove an item
  removeItem(index: number) {
    this.listItems.splice(index, 1);
  }
}
```

#### 3. HTML Templates

##### `src/app/text-editor.component.html`
```html
<div>
  <textarea #editor [innerHtml]="textContent" (input)="updateTextContent($event.target.value)" placeholder="Type here..."></textarea>
</div>

<button (click)="toggleListVisibility()">Toggle List</button>
<app-list-management *ngIf="showList"></app-list-management>
```

##### `src/app/list-management.component.html`
```html
<ul id="list-container">
  <li *ngFor="let listItem of listItems; let i = index">{{ listItem }}</li>
</ul>

<button (click)="addItem('New Item')">Add Item</button>
<button (click)="removeItem(0)">Remove First Item</button

